# Local machine + network config for scripts/install-ota.sh
#
#   cp scripts/ota.env.example scripts/ota.env    then fill it in
#
# scripts/ota.env is GITIGNORED and must stay that way. This repository is
# public, so none of the real values below belong in a commit: the tailnet
# hostname is publicly resolvable and would let a stranger probe the endpoint,
# and the device UDID is a hardware identifier for a phone you own.
# install-ota.sh refuses to run if ota.env has been added to git.

# SSH target for the host that publishes the install link (user@host).
# Careful: this is NOT automatically the same name as HOSTNAME_TS below. If
# Tailscale is stopped on this Mac, the .ts.net name resolves to the public
# Funnel ingress, which does not answer on port 22 — use the LAN address then,
# and the MagicDNS name only while this machine is actually on the tailnet.
PI="you@your-server.example"

# The Tailscale hostname the PHONE will fetch from, over the public internet.
# Must have Funnel enabled.
#   tailscale status --json | jq -r .Self.DNSName
HOSTNAME_TS="your-machine.tailnet-name.ts.net"

# The iPhone that will install this build. It must already be registered with
# your Apple Developer team, or the signed profile will not contain it and the
# install fails on the phone with an unhelpful message.
#   xcrun devicectl list devices
DEVICE_UDID="00000000-0000000000000000"

# ── Optional; the defaults are right unless you are sharing the host ────────
# TEAM_ID="XXXXXXXXXX"            # Apple Developer team, defaults to the one
#                                 # in scripts/update-hydra.sh
# BUNDLE_ID="com.example.hydra"   # App ID registered under that team
# FUNNEL_PATH="/hydra"            # path under :443 to mount on
# PORT="8791"                     # loopback port the file server binds to
# TTL="300"                       # seconds to keep the link up if nobody taps it
# GRACE="120"                     # seconds to keep it up after the phone pulls it
